==== jena-benchmark-jmh

The jena source release does not include large binary files.

The file "testing/data.nt.gz" is a placeholder for a large file for JMH testing. The file
name is known in various "Test*" classes.

Replace the file with a file of your choice, e.g. for BSBM - create "bsbm-5m.nt.gz".

The binary RDF benchmarks (org.apache.jena.riot.binary.TestBinaryRDFRead and
TestBinaryRDFWrite in jena-benchmarks-jmh, and org.apache.jena.grpc.BenchGrpcTransportJmh
in the jena-grpc test sources) read this placeholder by default. They take the file from
the system property "benchmark.source", so another file can be given without editing the
classes. From jena-benchmarks-jmh, after "mvn -Pdev install" of the checkout and
"mvn -DskipTests install" in jena-benchmarks:

    mvn -Dbenchmark.skip=false -Dtest=TestBinaryRDFRead test
    mvn -Dbenchmark.skip=false -Dtest=TestBinaryRDFWrite -Dbenchmark.source=/data/bsbm-5m.nt test

From the checkout root, for the gRPC transport benchmark:

    mvn -pl jena-grpc -Dbenchmark.skip=false -Dtest=BenchGrpcTransportJmh -Dbenchmark.source=/data/bsbm-5m.nt test

The format list of TestBinaryRDFRead and TestBinaryRDFWrite is the system property
"benchmark.formats": the names of RDFFormat constants, or "some.Class#FIELD" for a
constant on another class. With jelly-jena on the class path (it is a test dependency
of jena-benchmarks-jmh), Jelly-RDF is measured alongside the Jena formats like this:

    mvn -Dbenchmark.skip=false -Dtest=TestBinaryRDFRead -Dbenchmark.source=/data/bsbm-25m.nt \
        -Dbenchmark.formats=RDF_THRIFT,RDF_PROTO,eu.neverblink.jelly.convert.jena.riot.JellyFormat#JELLY_BIG_STRICT test

TestBinaryRDFRead writes the file in each format to a temporary file during setup and
times the read of it. TestBinaryRDFWrite and BenchGrpcTransportJmh hold the parsed
triples in memory, so their input has to fit in the heap as Triple objects: 5 million
triples need a few gigabytes. Each writes a JSON result file (jena-benchmarks-jmh:
Test*_<timestamp>.json in the module directory; jena-grpc: target/BenchGrpcTransportJmh.json).
